; A refused arrow stops the scope: the stage after it never fires.
;
; The call count is the proof, and `absent` cannot be — the deterministic
; calculus dumps the terms of the un-run expression, so an unfired prompt's own
; words still appear in the log. Counting is what distinguishes them.
;
; Three stages, two arrows. Unbroken that is 5 calls: three prompts and two
; checks. Refused at the first arrow it is 3: two prompts and the check that
; said no.
; expect: calls 3
(@ "Answer with exactly the single character: 0"
   (-> "Answer with exactly the word: alpha"
       "Repeat the word you were given, exactly."
       "Answer with exactly the word: unreachable"))
